      "message": "Hi @abror@google.com\n \nThank you for the review and for letting me know about the internal change.\n \nI\u0027ve filed a bug report as requested: https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/513076568\n \nIt includes production evidence from an Android 14 AAOS deployment (Qualcomm SA8255 IVI)\nshowing 15+ repeated DeadObjectException stack traces within 30 seconds from a single\nstale TunerSession, with no session cleanup ever triggered.\n \nI understand this CL may not be merged as-is since your team is working on an internal\nchange that builds upon this direction. To be honest, this was my first attempt at\ncontributing to AOSP, and I was really hoping to see it land ^^;— so it\u0027s a bit\nbittersweet. But what matters most is that the issue gets resolved properly for\nthe ecosystem, and I\u0027m glad it\u0027s moving in the right direction.\n \nIf there\u0027s anything I can help with — additional logs, testing on our AAOS devices,\nor reviewing the internal CL — please don\u0027t hesitate to reach out.\n \nBest regards",
